{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "OpenAPI Code Generation Demo",
  "description": "Demo flow: OpenAPI basics → Server APIs → NSwag client generation → Kiota client generation → Client usage → JavaScript clients",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "openapi-definition-demo/conference_openapi.yml",
      "line": 13,
      "title": "1. OpenAPI Definition",
      "description": "**Demo the OpenAPI spec** - This defines our Conference API with:\n- `/talks` endpoints (GET all, POST new, GET by id)\n- Request/response schemas\n- Status codes\n\nThis serves as the contract for both servers and generated clients."
    },
    {
      "directory": "openapi-definition-demo",
      "title": "2. OpenAPI Tooling (Swagger UI/Scalar)",
      "description": "**Demo Swagger UI and Scalar**\n\nShow:\n- Example request/response bodies\n- Multiple status codes\n- Schema definitions\n- Try it out (will get 401 - security not configured)\n- Scalar's 3-pane view and built-in API client\n\n🌐 Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger/, Scalar: http://localhost:8080/scalar/ (or open their `index.html` files straight from disk)\n\nMention: Postman can import this spec to generate a collection."
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceServerControllers/Controllers/TalksController.cs",
      "line": 23,
      "title": "3. Controllers API - ProducesResponseType",
      "description": "**Demo the Controllers-based API**\n\nKey points:\n- `[ProducesResponseType]` documents the OpenAPI spec\n- `IncludeOpenAPIAnalyzers` warns about undocumented status codes (try commenting line 34!)\n- XML comments enrich documentation\n\n🌐 Run with HTTPS: https://localhost:7135/scalar or https://localhost:7135/swagger"
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceServerControllers/Program.cs",
      "line": 15,
      "title": "4. OpenAPI document generation, Scalar & Swagger UI",
      "description": "**Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi + Scalar + Swagger UI**\n\n- Both servers generate an OpenAPI 3.1 document at `/openapi/v1.json` and show it with Scalar at `/scalar` and Swagger UI at `/swagger`\n- `[EndpointName(\"Talks_GetTalks\")]` on the controller actions (and `.WithName()` in the Minimal API) sets the `operationId`\n- Code generators use operationIds for method names: `NSwagTalksClient.GetTalksAsync()`, `talksGetTalks()`"
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/conference.nswag",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "5. NSwag - Configuration File",
      "description": "**Demo NSwag client generation**\n\nShow:\n- This `.nswag` file (can edit in NSwagStudio GUI)\n- Point to the OpenAPI document URL: https://localhost:7135/openapi/v1.json\n- Configure namespace, class name, output path"
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/Scripts/generate-nswag-client.ps1",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "6. NSwag - Generate via CLI",
      "description": "**Run NSwag generation**\n\n```powershell\n.\\Scripts\\generate-nswag-client.ps1\n```\n\nAlternatives:\n- NSwagStudio (GUI)\n- MSBuild integration\n- Direct `dotnet nswag` commands"
    },
    {
      "directory": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceApp/Clients/NSwag",
      "title": "7. NSwag - Generated Client",
      "description": "**Show the generated NSwag client**\n\n- Single file with all client code\n- Strongly-typed methods: `GetTalksAsync()`, `GetTalkAsync(id)`, `CreateTalkAsync()`\n- Models generated from OpenAPI schemas"
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/Scripts/generate-kiota-client.ps1",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "8. Kiota - CLI Generation",
      "description": "**Demo Kiota CLI**\n\nShow the command:\n```powershell\n.\\Scripts\\generate-kiota-client.ps1\n```\n\nOr use `kiota show` for a tree view of the API.\n\nAlternative: **Kiota VS Code extension** (GitHub integration)"
    },
    {
      "directory": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceApp/Clients/Kiota",
      "title": "9. Kiota - Generated Client",
      "description": "**Show the generated Kiota client**\n\n- Modular structure (separate files for models, builders)\n- Fluent API following URL structure\n- `kiota-lock.json` tracks generation config"
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceApp/Program.cs",
      "line": 16,
      "title": "10. NSwag Client Usage",
      "description": "**Demo using NSwag client**\n\n```csharp\nvar client = new NSwagTalksClient(httpClient);\nvar talks = await client.GetTalksAsync();\nvar talk = await client.GetTalkAsync(1);\n```\n\nTraditional, straightforward API style."
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceApp/Program.cs",
      "line": 31,
      "title": "11. Kiota Client Usage",
      "description": "**Demo using Kiota client**\n\n```csharp\nvar client = new KiotaConferenceClient(adapter);\nvar talks = await client.Api.Talks.GetAsync();\nvar talk = await client.Api.Talks[1].GetAsync();\n```\n\nFluent builder pattern with indexer syntax for IDs."
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceAppJs/package.json",
      "line": 8,
      "title": "12. JavaScript - Generate clients",
      "description": "**Generate the JavaScript clients**\n\n```powershell\ncd api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceAppJs\nnpm install\nnpm run generate\n```\n\n- `openapi-typescript`: types only (`schema.d.ts`)\n- Hey API: `openapi-ts.config.ts` → SDK functions + types\n- Orval: `orval.config.ts` → fetch functions (can also do TanStack Query, Zod, MSW mocks)"
    },
    {
      "directory": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceAppJs/src/clients",
      "title": "13. JavaScript - Generated clients",
      "description": "**Compare the generated output**\n\n- `openapi-typescript/schema.d.ts`: a single `paths` type, no runtime code\n- `hey-api/`: SDK functions named after the operationIds (`talksGetTalks`) plus a bundled fetch client\n- `orval/conference.ts`: one file with fetch functions and response types per status code"
    },
    {
      "file": "api-client-generation-demo/ConferenceAppJs/src/index.ts",
      "line": 13,
      "title": "14. JavaScript - Client usage",
      "description": "**Demo the JavaScript clients**\n\n```powershell\nnpm start\n```\n\n- openapi-fetch: `client.GET('/api/talks/{id}', { params: { path: { id: 1 } } })`\n- Hey API: `talksGetTalk({ path: { id: 1 } })`\n- Orval: `talksGetTalk(1)`"
    }
  ]
}